        "content": "## Send cold outreach from an uploaded lead file and detect replies in Gmail\n\n**Who's it for**\nSmall sales teams running cold email who want three things joined up: importing a lead list,\nsending the first touch, and knowing the moment somebody replies with interest - without watching\nan inbox.\n\n**How it works**\nThree flows around one lead table.\n\n**Import** - upload a CSV or spreadsheet through the form. The rows are read and upserted into the\nlead table, so re-uploading a corrected file updates people rather than duplicating them.\n\n**Send** - on a schedule, or on demand, the offer settings are loaded and the leads not yet\ncontacted are read. Each gets the outreach email through Gmail, the sent message is recorded, and\nthe lead row is marked contacted. Marking after the send is what stops a crash re-mailing anyone.\n\n**Reply detection** - a Gmail trigger fires on an incoming message. It is matched back to a lead,\nstored, and the whole thread is pulled so the classifier reads the conversation rather than one\nmessage. Only the prospect's own messages are kept - feeding your own sent copy back to the model\nis how a reply classifier convinces itself every thread is interested. An AI agent returns a typed\nclassification against a fixed schema, and an interested prospect is flagged for human handoff.\n\n**How to set up**\n1. Attach Gmail credentials to the send node and the trigger, and set the sender address.\n2. Fill in **`config: the offer`** with your offer, subject line and email body.\n3. Create the data tables for leads, sent messages and received messages.\n4. Attach an OpenRouter credential to the model node.\n\n**Requirements**\nA Gmail account, an OpenRouter API key, and n8n data tables for leads and messages.\n\n**How to customize**\nThe email copy lives in **`config: the offer`**. What counts as interested is the prompt on\n**`classify the reply`** plus **`reply classification schema`** - change them together."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-01",
      "name": "1. Import the leads",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -264
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 224,
        "content": "### 1. Import the leads\n\nUpload a CSV or spreadsheet through the form. **`read the lead file`** parses it and **`store the leads`** upserts each row.\n\nUpsert, not insert: re-uploading a corrected file updates those people instead of creating a second copy of your list."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-02",
      "name": "2. Send the first touch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        280,
        910
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1320,
        "height": 202,
        "content": "### 2. Send the first touch\n\n**`config: the offer`** holds the offer, subject and body in one node - it is the only place you edit copy.\n\n**`read leads not yet contacted`** is what makes the pass repeatable, and the row is marked **after** the send succeeds. Marking first would silently drop anyone the send failed for."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-03",
      "name": "3. Read the thread, not the message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -542
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1320,
        "height": 202,
        "content": "### 3. Read the thread, not the message\n\nA reply is matched back to a lead, stored, and then the **whole thread** is pulled.\n\n**`keep only the prospect's messages`** drops your own sent copy before the model sees it. Leaving it in is how a reply classifier talks itself into scoring every thread as interested - it is reading your pitch back to itself."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-04",
      "name": "4. Typed classification, human handoff",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1400,
        1210
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 224,
        "content": "### 4. Typed classification, then a human\n\n**`classify the reply`** is pinned by **`reply classification schema`**, so the verdict is a typed field rather than a sentence somebody has to interpret.\n\nAn interested prospect is **flagged for handoff**, not auto-replied to. The first real conversation is the one worth a person."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
